# Personal Trading Intelligence — environment configuration
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust if needed.
#
# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SQLite path is resolved RELATIVE to prisma/schema.prisma, so "../db/custom.db"
# keeps the database inside the project's db/ folder for development.
#
# The packaged desktop app does NOT use this file: the Electron shell sets
# DATABASE_URL to the user-data directory (%APPDATA%\TradingIntelligence\data)
# and migrates the schema automatically on first start (see src/lib/db-bootstrap.ts).

DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"

# ─── Desktop build (set automatically by desktop-build/main.js) ──────────────
# PTI_DATA_DIR      user-data folder that holds the database + sync token
# PTI_TOKEN_FILE    file storing the per-launch MT5 sync token (X-PTI-Token)
# PTI_LOG_DIR       connector + desktop log folder
# PTI_PYTHON        bundled python.exe path
# PTI_SYNC_SCRIPT   bundled sync_service.py path

# ─── MT5 sync API security (optional overrides) ──────────────────────────────
# Hard-coded sync token instead of the per-launch token file:
# PTI_SYNC_TOKEN=
# Force token enforcement even in dev (default: token required only when one
# has been configured — desktop always configures one):
# PTI_REQUIRE_TOKEN=1
